    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Apply / update / cancel matting stroke on a video or photo segment.\r\nPass exactly one of --enable / --disable.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type(s): video, audio, text, sticker\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --enable            Enable the matting stroke\r\n          --disable           Disable / cancel the matting stroke\r\n          --resource TEXT     Stroke resource: vimo://<id> (vimo only)\r\n          --color TEXT        Stroke color: #RRGGBB[AA] / r,g,b[,a]\r\n          --stroke TEXT       Stroke size (float), maps to effects_adjust_size. Unitless\r\n                              scalar.\r\n          --alpha TEXT        Stroke alpha (float), maps to effects_adjust_alpha. Use a bare\r\n                              scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is invalid. Range after\r\n                              normalization: [0,1].\r\n          --distance TEXT     Stroke distance (float), maps to effects_adjust_distance.\r\n                              Unitless scalar.\r\n          --shadow TEXT       Stroke shadow/texture (float), maps to effects_adjust_shadow.\r\n                              Unitless scalar.\r\n          --texture TEXT      Alias of --shadow for texture-style stroke sliders. Unitless\r\n                              scalar.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: matting-stroke only applies to video/photo segments; resource must be vimo://.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Enable a matting stroke with a resource and stroke size (color/alpha optional)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video matting-stroke --seg-id <UUID> --enable --resource vimo://7172457125392683528 --stroke 0.35 --distance 1 --texture 1\r\n  # Disable / cancel the matting stroke\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video matting-stroke --seg-id <UUID> --disable\r\n",
